---
import numbers from "../data/numbers.json";
const meta = numbers.report_snippet;
---

<section id="report" class="border-t border-line py-20 sm:py-28" aria-labelledby="report-heading">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker mb-5"><span class="num">05</span> An example report</p>
    <h2 id="report-heading" class="font-serif italic font-semibold text-section leading-[1.1] max-w-3xl">
      Every finding carries evidence and a command you can paste.
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-paper/90">
      This is a real report, not a mock-up. It was produced by running Aethens on a planted
      test-order defect in the self-authored bench. {meta.label}. Tool aethens {meta.tool_version},
      budget {meta.budget}, seed {meta.seed}. Duration on that machine was 32.1 seconds and will
      vary.
    </p>
    <p class="cmd-label mt-8">Reproduce this report</p>
    <pre class="cmd max-w-3xl" tabindex="0"><code>{meta.command}</code></pre>

    <article class="report mt-10 max-w-4xl" aria-label="Aethens report for order-alphabetical">
      <header class="report-head">
        <div>
          <p class="font-mono text-[0.68rem] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-gold">Aethens report</p>
          <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs text-muted">
            Tool aethens {meta.tool_version} · Budget: {meta.budget} · Seed: {meta.seed} · Checks run: C005 · Tasks: 1 · Duration: 32.1s
          </p>
        </div>
        <p class="sev-error"><span class="sev-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>1 error, 0 warning, 0 info</p>
      </header>

      <div class="scroll-x border-0 border-b border-line">
        <table class="sheet">
          <caption class="sr-only">Findings summary</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Severity</th>
              <th scope="col">Check</th>
              <th scope="col">Task</th>
              <th scope="col">Title</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td class="sev-error">error</td>
              <td class="font-mono text-sm">C005</td>
              <td class="font-mono text-sm">order-alphabetical</td>
              <td>Test verdict depends on test order or isolation: test_reg.TestRegistry.test_b_lookup</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="p-5 sm:p-6 space-y-4">
        <h3 class="font-serif italic text-xl">
          <span class="sev-error not-italic">error</span>
          <span class="font-mono not-italic text-sm text-muted mx-2">C005</span>
          order-alphabetical
        </h3>
        <p class="text-paper/90">
          test_reg.TestRegistry.test_b_lookup gives 'pass' in the verifier's default order but a
          different verdict in reversed order: error; in shuffled order (driver seed 4228934073):
          error; alone in a fresh process: error. It passes only because of state left behind by
          tests that run before it in the default order (or it is broken by tests that run before it
          in another order). Solutions are judged by an accident of test order. Both the baseline
          and the changed order were run twice with the same PYTHONHASHSEED and gave the same
          verdicts.
        </p>
        <ul class="text-sm space-y-1 text-paper/85 font-mono text-[0.8rem] leading-relaxed">
          <li>Observed: default order: pass; in reversed order: error</li>
          <li>Subject: <code>test:test_reg.TestRegistry.test_b_lookup</code>; confidence: <code>confirmed</code>; seed: <code>0</code></li>
          <li>Command: <code>python .aethens/order_driver.py reverse -- discover -s tests</code></li>
          <li class="text-muted whitespace-normal font-sans text-sm">
            Limits: Orders tried: default, reversed, 1 seeded shuffle(s) and up to 10 tests alone
            (budget smoke). Dependence that only shows in an order not tried is missed, and so is a
            run that crashes before reporting per-test verdicts. The driver adds .aethens/ to the
            work directory; tests that list the work directory could notice it.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <div>
          <p class="cmd-label">Reproduce</p>
          <pre class="cmd" tabindex="0"><code>aethens audit bench/tasks/order-alphabetical --check C005 --seed 0 --budget smoke</code></pre>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="cmd-label">stderr (tail)</p>
          <pre class="cmd" tabindex="0"><code>test_b_lookup (test_reg.TestRegistry.test_b_lookup) ... ERROR
test_a_register (test_reg.TestRegistry.test_a_register) ... ok

======================================================================
ERROR: test_b_lookup (test_reg.TestRegistry.test_b_lookup)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Traceback (most recent call last):
  File "/work/tests/test_reg.py", line 14, in test_b_lookup
    self.assertEqual(lookup("x"), 1)
                     ^^^^^^^^^^^
  File "/work/reg.py", line 9, in lookup
    return _REGISTRY[name]
           ~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^
KeyError: 'x'

----------------------------------------------------------------------
Ran 2 tests in 0.001s

FAILED (errors=1)</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-sm text-muted">
      The full markdown, exactly as the CLI printed it, is checked into{' '}
      <code class="text-gold">data/report-order-alphabetical.md</code>
      {' '}in this website repository. A shorter C001 example on{' '}
      <code class="text-gold">brokengold-offbyone</code> is in{' '}
      <code class="text-gold">data/report-brokengold-offbyone.md</code>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
